{
  "summary": "Adds wallet and RPC support for sending transactions to BIP 352 Silent Payment addresses across send, sendtoaddress, sendmany, and sendall. It introduces PaymentDestination to handle addresses whose taproot scriptPubKeys are derived dynamically from selected transaction inputs, updates coin selection to ensure derivation-eligible keys are present and spendable, and writes silent payment recipient metadata to wallet storage so transactions can be RBF fee-bumped.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core cannot send funds to BIP 352 silent payment addresses. Users who want the privacy and address-reuse prevention benefits of silent payments cannot pay silent payment recipients using Bitcoin Core wallet RPCs or the GUI.",
  "evidence": [
    "Part of the BIP 352 silent payments project tracked under issue #28536, following the previous iteration in PR #28201.",
    "BIP 352 addresses require dynamic scriptPubKey generation from the inputs' private keys, necessitating custom coin selection, wallet storage of recipient data (sprecipients) for RBF re-derivation, and disabling incompatible features like PSBT and offline signers for these sends (PR description)."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#35301"
    ],
    "enables": [
      "#32966"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches core wallet transaction construction, coin selection, fee bumping, wallet database records, and RPC parsing; introduces a Python BIP 352 scanning implementation in the test framework.",
  "changed_since_previous": "The core approach remains unchanged, retaining PaymentDestination, input-dependent coin selection, and recipient persistence for RBF.",
  "card": "Adds wallet and RPC support for sending to BIP 352 Silent Payment addresses across send, sendtoaddress, sendmany, and sendall. Currently, Bitcoin Core wallet users cannot pay silent payment addresses, preventing the use of receiver privacy protocols. The PR introduces PaymentDestination for dynamic output derivation, updates coin selection to ensure eligible private keys are available, and stores recipient destinations in the wallet database to support RBF fee bumping. This work is tracked under issue #28536, depends on prerequisite PR #35301, and helps unblock receiving support in PR #32966.",
